## What I could not do / notes

- **Leg 2 cannot run in this worktree**: it is not clean and cannot be made clean by me — other workers hold modified tracked files under `008-command-surfacing-build/` and the runner/scorer themselves are untracked. I ran the identical command against `git clone` of HEAD in `/tmp` with the runner copied into the gitignored `runtime/dist/routing-accuracy/`, which gives a genuinely clean tree; the clone was deleted afterwards. The orchestrator should re-run leg 2 literally after the runner is committed.
- That clone run exposed a real defect I fixed: the exempt-prefix check compared two spellings of a path, so a symlinked root (`/tmp` → `/private/tmp`) classified every path as dirty. It now asks git for `rev-parse --show-prefix` of the out folder, with no path-string comparison.
- One judgement call to flag: T012's line presupposes prompt lookup by `--row-id`, so I implemented lookup plus the `holdout` refusal; T013's description repeats that refusal. T013's `--set chat|g2`, `--list`, `--set` fixtures and started-set cap are untouched.
- Nothing committed or pushed, no git state touched (the temp clone excepted and removed), `tasks.md` not ticked, no files written outside the named script.
